Theorem RL-34: tail-call preservation — never RcDec after a tail call; transfer only when callee Owned

  Preconditions:
    - RL-34 governs tail-call preservation per Annex E §AIMS Borrow
      Inference: "Never insert RcDec after a tail call. Transfer ownership
      instead — BUT only when the callee parameter is Owned. Callee Borrowed
      -> ownership transfer violates the ABI (the callee expects a borrow, the
      caller's dec never fires -> leak). Cannot tail-call to Borrowed unless
      the caller arranges the dec before the call."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - An RcDec after a tail call breaks TCO (tail-call optimization); the
      Lean 4 ownParamsUsingArgs lineage (Annex E §AIMS §8
      Patterns) transfers ownership instead.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-3 ParamContract.access (the callee param ABI).

  Soundness property:
    Forall tail call passing v to a callee parameter:

      (P1) Action decision: when the callee param is Owned, RL-34 transfers
           ownership of v to the callee (no post-call RcDec — TCO preserved).
           When the callee param is Borrowed, RL-34 emits the RcDec BEFORE the
           call (ownership cannot transfer to a Borrowed param).

      (P2) Soundness: an RcDec AFTER a tail call would break TCO (the tail
           position is no longer the last operation). Transferring ownership
           to an Owned param is correct (the callee will dec). Transferring to
           a Borrowed param would leak (the callee never decs a borrow, and
           the caller's post-call dec is forbidden) — so the caller must dec
           before the call instead. In NO case is an RcDec inserted after the
           tail call.

    RL-34 preserves both TCO and RC balance: ownership transfer where the
    callee owns, pre-call dec where it borrows, never a post-call dec.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — tail-call action cases:
      callee Owned -> TransferOwnership (no post-call dec; TCO preserved)
      callee Borrowed -> DecBeforeCall (cannot transfer; dec pre-call)
      Coverage gate: 2 action cases. Negative-direction witness: an RcDec is
      NEVER inserted after a tail call (it breaks TCO) — the action is always
      either pre-call transfer or pre-call dec; the post-call-dec branch is
      asserted unreachable.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl34_tail_call_preservation;
        tail-call action enumeration + never-post-call-dec witness; emits Fail
        on a wrong action or a post-call dec)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-34 via the tail-call action cases (callee Owned -> transfer ownership, TCO preserved; callee Borrowed -> dec before the call) with a negative-direction witness confirming an RcDec is never inserted after a tail call, preserving both TCO and RC balance
